                 Computer/Practice Chanter Alignment Window
                      _________________________________    


        This window creates the file "chanter.txt" needed by the Win(d)Bag
program to play the notes of your practice chanter.  

	Each Scroll bar represents the frequency of the note that is beside
it.  To change the pitches scroll the Low G bar.  As you adjust the Low G
scroll bar to a different frequency all the other bars will adjust to match
the proper intervals of the bagpipe scale.  When you are satisfied that Low 
G is ok then move on to Low A.  As Low A is adjusted B,C,D,E,F,high G, and 
High A are adjusted accordingly.  Low G is not adjusted.  In this manner go 
up the scale to High A.  when you are satisfied with the notes press the 
"Thumbs up" radio button.

        To stop the tone at any time press the "halt hand" radio button.

        This window only needs to be used once unless the pitch of your 
practice chanter changes.
        
